{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And all the wells which they had dug.</b> Scripture tells that out of the jealousy the Philistines bore toward him, they stopped up all the wells which they had dug in the days of Abraham his father, so that Isaac would not be able to benefit from them and to water his sowings and his flocks. Afterward Isaac prevailed and dug them and called them by the names which his father had called them, and he did so for his father's honor. And from the fact that the Torah made this known, it appears that it was reckoned to him as merit, and in this there is an arousal and all the more so (קל וחומר) that a person should not deviate from the way of his fathers — since Isaac did not wish to change even the names of the wells which his father had called them, and this is all the more so regarding the ways of the fathers and their customs and their discipline. And perhaps for this reason his name was not changed, unlike the other fathers, and this is measure for measure; thus explained the Gaon, of blessed memory." "<b>And there are those</b> who explained that these wells allude to the converts who converted in the days of Abraham, for they are receptive to the acceptance of faith just as wells are receptive to the receiving of water, and the opening of the heart that is closed to faith the Scripture calls 'digging.' And therefore it says that out of jealousy the Philistines stopped them up — that is, they stopped up their heart and turned them back to their former state — and this is ״וימלאום עפר״, for instead of Abraham having filled them with wisdom and knowledge of HaShem in the faith of unity, the Philistines filled them with their evil faith. For Scripture calls evil faith or evil counsel ״עפר״, and this is what they said: עפרא לפומיה. And afterward Isaac prevailed over them and restored them to the good, which is what is written: ״וישב יצחק ויחפור את בארות המים אשר חפרו בימי אברהם אביו ויסתמום פלשתים אחרי מות אברהם ויקרא להן שמות כשמות״ וגו', for such is the way of converts, as in the matter that is written (Isaiah 65:15): ״ולעבדיו יקרא שם אחר״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:25.281046364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}